A duration is derived from the effort the plan already carries, never declared
beside it (`A1-147`, ADR-0023). One number is configured, `effort_days_per_week`,
and every surface divides the effort on the row by it. Nothing is said about
dates: a week here is a unit of capacity, not a position in a calendar.

```
$ aplan summary
phase  tasks  done  effort
    0      4     1    7.0d
total      4     1    7.0d

at 5.0 effort days a week: 1.4 weeks of work, 1.2 remaining
ready: 2

```

The roadmap states the assumption once, then divides each cut's own effort by it.
The header is what the rows add up to -- every cut that is not a release, plus the
work in no cut -- so it reconciles against `summary` above without arithmetic.
`(1.0w left)` is what is still to do, so a cut whose work is finished reads as
zero rather than disappearing.

```
$ aplan roadmap
roadmap: 1 cut(s), 4 task(s), 7.0d effort
throughput: 5.0 effort days a week

v0.1  Core  [todo]  1/3 done, 1 ready, 1 blocked, crit 5.0d, 6.0d effort, 1.2w (1.0w left)
  Alpha       todo          Alpha task
  Beta        done          Beta task
  Gamma       todo          Gamma task

cross-cutting (in no cut): 1.0d effort, 0.2w (0.2w left)
  Xtra        todo          Cross gate

(statuses are as claimed in the plan and gated by `aplan verify` in CI)

```

The markdown table grows a `weeks` column only here: a repository that declares
no throughput renders the table it always did. The first cell is untouched
either way, which is what ADR-0015 resolves a `traces` row anchor by.

```
$ aplan roadmap --format markdown
<!-- generated by `aplan roadmap --format markdown`; do not edit. -->
<!-- regenerate: `aplan roadmap --format markdown` -->

# Roadmap

## Cuts

| cut | status | done/total | ready | blocked | effort | weeks | critical path |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| v0.1 | todo | 1/3 | 1 | 1 | 6.0d | 1.2 (1.0 left) | 5.0d |

## v0.1 Core

| task | title | status | blocked_by | evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Alpha | Alpha task | todo | - | - |
| Beta | Beta task | done | - | commit:abc1234 |
| Gamma | Gamma task | todo | Alpha | - |

## Cross-cutting (in no cut)

1.0d effort, 0.2 weeks (0.2 left), held by tasks in no cut and not counted in the table above.

| task | title | status | blocked_by | evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Xtra | Cross gate | todo | - | - |

> Statuses are as claimed in the plan and gated by `aplan verify` in CI.

```

A throughput nothing can be divided by is refused at load rather than ignored:
the alternative is a repository declaring one thing and the tool doing another.

```
$ aplan --root zero summary
? 2
aplan: invalid `effort_days_per_week` in `.aplan.yml`: it is `0`; it must be a positive number of effort days a week (e.g. `5` for one person, or `7.5` for five days at an assumed 1.5x)

```
